the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Irregular Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the Past Simple tense to talk about actions that happened in the past.<br/><br/>To form the Past Simple tense of a <span class=\"italic\">regular</span> verb, you follow certain rules.<br/><br/>Some verbs do not follow any rules. They are called <span class=\"italic\">irregular verbs</span>. Here are the past tense forms of some irregular verbs:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes the verb changes completely:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">think</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">be</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">thought</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">was</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes there is \\\"half\\\" a change:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">write</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">do</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">wrote</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">did</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes there is no change:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">read</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">read</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I thought I heard the 20th. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I read that the card was for all new employees. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The receptionist told me to come here. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wrote down the wrong address.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking for Clarification", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "  If you don't understand what a person is saying, it is important to ask for clarification in a polite way. <br/><br/>  One way to ask for clarification is to ask the person to repeat what they said.<br/><br/>  Here are some phrases and expressions you can use to ask for repetition or clarification:<br/><br/>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " <ul> <li><span class=\"italic\">Excuse me?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Could you repeat that?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Could you say that again?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">What did you say?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">What was that (again)?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Did you say . . . ?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">I'm sorry. I didn't catch that.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Is it X or Y? *</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Is that correct?</span></li> </ul><br/><br/> *<span class=\"italic\">If you want to clarify between two things, you can ask if it's (X) or (Y)?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm sorry. I'm not quite sure I caught that. Can you repeat that please?", "type": "example"}, {"content": " Is Cathy spelled with a C or K? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Did you say 289?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "visitor's pass", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a small card that is used by someone who doesn't work in a specific building ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will need a visitor's pass. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about entering an office building.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "access card", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a plastic card used to provide access to a building ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am a new employee. I need to get an access card.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "front entrance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the main doors you go through at the front to enter a building ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Use this card when you enter through the front entrance. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "back door", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a door at the back or side of a building ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  You can use the back door as well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to punch in", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to push buttons on a machine ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to punch in the numbers in the morning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "code", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a set of numbers you use to open something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Punch in the code to open the door.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Pretend you just started a new job. You are finishing your first day.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 10 - 12 sentences about what happened. What did you do? How did you feel? Who did you meet? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Circle all the verbs in the Simple Past tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your sentences. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading them aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about actions and events in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about a day at work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about actions related to work.", "type": "text"}]}]}